{"season":2026,"week":10,"kind":"preview","league":"67FFL","my_team":"ATX Bowers","generated_utc":"2026-11-12T22:46Z","writer":"claude","headline":"Week 10 preview: fill the kicker hole, start Estime, look at Kamara","dek":"Your lineup projects at 108.0 with an empty slot, and a trade with Game of Throws could add about two points before the week 11 deadline.","sections":[{"id":"my_lineup","title":"Your best lineup","md":"Our projection has your best lineup at **108.0**, and that total includes a zero. One slot is empty, almost certainly kicker, since Cairo Santos is on bye. Jonah Coleman is also on bye, but he wasn't in your best lineup anyway.\n\n- **QB:** Drake Maye (18.23)\n- **RB:** Tony Pollard (16.01), Audric Estime (10.27)\n- **WR:** Rashee Rice (12.16), Deebo Samuel Sr. (10.99)\n- **TE:** Dalton Kincaid (9.79)\n- **FLEX:** Denzel Boston (10.84), Brenton Strange (9.58)\n- **DEF:** BAL D/ST (10.11)\n\nInjury notes to check before kickoff:\n- **Denzel Boston** did not practice (toe). He's the one to watch, and Tank Dell is the obvious fallback at flex.\n- **Deebo Samuel Sr.** (hamstring) and **Dalton Kincaid** (ankle) were limited.\n- Drake Maye (shoulder), Tony Pollard (finger) and Rashee Rice (knee) all practiced fully.\n\nThe easiest points this week are at kicker. The top waiver options project around 9 (see waivers), which would lift your total to roughly 117."},{"id":"close_calls","title":"Close calls","md":"**FLEX: Brenton Strange over Tank Dell (9.58 vs 9.28)**\n\nThis is close to a coin flip, and the signals are mixed.\n- **Strange:** he sits in the best game environment, with JAX implied at **28.5** against TEN. But his last three games average 7.0, his xFP over that span is 6.1, and his snap share has slipped from 75% to 69%.\n- **Dell:** he has the stronger recent usage, with xFP of 9.7 and 14% target share. But that's only 2 games, he plays 35% of snaps, HOU is implied at just 22.5 against CLE, and he's limited with a hand injury.\n\nI'd stick with Strange unless Boston's toe forces a change. In that case, check whether Dell's hand and Strange's matchup still make sense for the second flex.\n\n**RB: Audric Estime over Aaron Jones (10.27 vs 9.21)**\n\nHere the pre-game signals agree with our projection.\n- **Estime:** NO is implied at 25.5 against CAR, and his xFP over the last three is 8.7.\n- **Jones:** his snap share has dropped from 58% on the season to 33% over the last three, his last-three average is 4.2 (xFP 4.9), and MIN is implied at only 19.2 against GB.\n\nEstime has just 2 games of data and a 2% target share, so he is touchdown-dependent in PPR. Even so, Jones' usage trend points the wrong way."},{"id":"waivers","title":"Waiver adds and streamers","md":"**Kicker comes first.** An empty slot costs you about 9 points.\n- **Brandon McManus** (LA): 9.07\n- **Harrison Mevis** (LA): 9.03\n- **Charlie Smyth** (NO): 8.85\n- **Eddy Pineiro** (SF): 8.65\n\nMcManus and Mevis project almost identically and play for the same team, so take whichever is available.\n\n**WR: Devaughn Vele (NO), 11.07.** He would project above both Boston (10.84) and Samuel (10.99). He plays 92% of snaps, has a 15% target share, and NO is implied at 25.5 against CAR. He's the best add if Boston's toe is a problem.\n\nAdonai Mitchell (NYJ, 9.90) is worth a look. His xFP over the last three is 13.4, well above his projection, and he has a 21% target share.\n\n**RB (your position of need):** your RB strength of 26.3 is below the league median of 32.5.\n- **Dylan Sampson** (CLE, 8.81): his snaps have risen from 42% to 55%, his xFP over the last three is 10.2, and he has a 16% target share. The catch is that CLE is implied at only 18.0.\n- **Devin Singletary** (NYG, 9.34): he's at 54% of snaps over the last three, with xFP of 8.3.\n\nNeither beats your current starters this week, so treat them as depth while Jonah Coleman is on bye.\n\n**QB, TE and D/ST** don't need streaming. Maye (18.23), Kincaid and Strange, and BAL D/ST (10.11) all project above the best available options."},{"id":"buy_sell","title":"Buy low, sell high","md":"Two of your players are outscoring their expected fantasy points (xFP), and two are underperforming theirs. The trade deadline is **week 11**, so the window to act is nearly closed.\n\n**Sell high**\n- **Deebo Samuel Sr.:** 12.1 PPR per game against 9.0 xFP, a gap of **+3.1**. He's also limited with a hamstring.\n- **Rashee Rice:** 13.2 PPR per game against 10.3 xFP, a gap of **+2.9**.\n\nOur projection already prices both below their scoring averages (10.99 and 12.16). If a buyer pays for the averages, that's the case for selling. Both are in your starting lineup, so you'd need a replacement.\n\n**Hold or buy low**\n- **Jordan Addison:** 7.7 per game against 9.0 xFP (**-1.3**).\n- **Jonah Coleman:** 12.6 per game against 13.7 xFP (**-1.1**), and he's on bye this week.\n\nBoth are producing a bit less than their usage suggests. The gaps are small, so don't read too much into them."},{"id":"around_league","title":"Around the league: needs and trade fits","md":"**The one fit the numbers found:** Game of Throws would give you **Alvin Kamara** (RB, NO, 11.48) for **Tank Dell** (WR, HOU, 9.28).\n- **Your side:** you need a running back. Kamara would become your RB2 and push Estime into the flex, replacing Strange. That's worth about **1.9** points a week. Dell isn't in your lineup, so you give up depth rather than a starter. Kamara and Estime are both on NO, so you'd be doubling up on one team.\n- **Their side:** they have the league's deepest RB group (62.4) but a WR group of just 9.4, against a league median of 37.5. They also need a QB. Dell fills a real hole for them.\n- **Worth knowing:** Dell is limited with a hand injury. Raise that if the other manager asks about his health.\n\nWorth a look before the week 11 deadline.\n\n**Other ideas, with no fit flagged:**\n- **Tight end:** your TE strength is 19.4 against a median of 11.6. Chentudo El Venudo (TE 8.1), Bucky Charms (7.8) and Sebas350 (5.6) all list TE as a need. Strange is filling your second flex, though, so you'd lose something.\n- **Running back:** Moore Than A Bite has a deep RB group (56.5) and lists Tyler Allgeier (10.24) as surplus, but they currently show no needs for you to fill.\n- **Competition for RBs:** The Dakstreet Boys, I Love it Ra and Lover Boys all list RB as a need. Lover Boys have TreVeyon Henderson out with illness.\n\n**League snapshot:** Just Win Baby (8-1, 139.6 projected) lead the league and list QB as their only need. Chentudo El Venudo (7-2) and Moore Than A Bite (6-3) follow. You're at 1-8, and your 108.0 projection ranks 10th of 12 before you fill the kicker slot."}],"links":{"Drake Maye":"p:00-0039851","Tony Pollard":"p:00-0035261","Audric Estime":"p:00-0039373","Rashee Rice":"p:00-0039067","Deebo Samuel Sr.":"p:00-0035719","Dalton Kincaid":"p:00-0038933","BAL D/ST":"d:BAL","Denzel Boston":"p:00-0041037","Brenton Strange":"p:00-0038935","Jonah Coleman":"p:00-0041496","Cairo Santos":"p:00-0031203","Tank Dell":"p:00-0038977","Aaron Jones":"p:00-0033293","Matthew Stafford":"p:00-0026498","Sam Darnold":"p:00-0034869","Kyler Murray":"p:00-0035228","Deshaun Watson":"p:00-0033537","Devin Singletary":"p:00-0035250","Dylan Sampson":"p:00-0040162","Ty Johnson":"p:00-0035537","MarShawn Lloyd":"p:00-0039811","Devaughn Vele":"p:00-0039424","Adonai Mitchell":"p:00-0039890","Xavier Hutchinson":"p:00-0038618","Malachi Fields":"p:00-0041042","AJ Barner":"p:00-0039793","Tyler Higbee":"p:00-0033110","Dalton Schultz":"p:00-0034383","Pat Freiermuth":"p:00-0036894","Brandon McManus":"p:00-0029822","Harrison Mevis":"p:00-0039498","Charlie Smyth":"p:00-0039229","Eddy Pineiro":"p:00-0034173","WAS D/ST":"d:WAS","NYG D/ST":"d:NYG","MIA D/ST":"d:MIA","LAC D/ST":"d:LAC","Jordan Addison":"p:00-0038994","Garrett Wilson":"p:00-0037740","KC Concepcion":"p:00-0041547","Chris Rodriguez Jr.":"p:00-0038611","RJ Harvey":"p:00-0040730","Tyler Allgeier":"p:00-0037263","DJ Moore":"p:00